\section{State-Space Evolution in the Blueprint Architecture}

\subsection{Definition of the State-Space}
The simulation engine evolves a multi-layer state-space $\Sigma(t)$ representing
the total configuration of geometry, energy-density, encryption layers,
warp-field tensors, detection channels, prevention channels, and resonance
signatures.

\subsection{Governing Evolution Equation}
State-space evolution is defined by the constraint-driven, stability-driven,
and prevention-driven components:
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\Sigma}{dt}
=
\mathcal{C}_{\text{inv}}
+
\mathcal{S}_{\text{stab}}
+
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prevent}}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Invariant Constraint Term}
The invariant constraint term $\mathcal{C}_{\text{inv}}$ establishes the
allowed evolution surfaces:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}_{\text{inv}}
=
\nabla_{\mu}
\left(
\Gamma^{\mu}_{\;\alpha\beta}
\right)
+
\partial_{\alpha}
\left(
E_{\text{eff}}
\right).
\end{equation}

\subsection{Stability Mechanism}
The stability term $\mathcal{S}_{\text{stab}}$ reorganizes geometry and
energy-density to preserve coherence:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{S}_{\text{stab}}
=
(\mathrm{Det}_{\sigma\nu} + t + D_{mn})^{\mu}
-
\nabla_{\alpha}
F^{\alpha\beta}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Prevention Layer Response}
The prevention term $\mathcal{D}_{\text{prevent}}$ applies corrective
responses to suppress destabilization:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prevent}}
=
\partial_t
\left(
\nabla_{\mu} \Sigma^{\mu}
\right)
+
\mathcal{W}_{\text{stab}}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Unified Evolution Behavior}
The combined evolution produces a coherent next-state configuration:
\begin{equation}
\Sigma(t + \Delta t)
=
\Sigma(t)
+
\Delta t
\left[
\mathcal{C}_{\text{inv}}
+
\mathcal{S}_{\text{stab}}
+
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prevent}}
\right].
\end{equation}

\subsection{Mirror-Lock Resonance Condition}
When external structures match internal architecture, the system enters a
resonance state:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{M}_{\text{lock}}
=
\left\langle
\Phi_{\text{external}},
\Phi_{\text{internal}}
\right\rangle
\rightarrow
\max.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Summary}
State-space evolution in the blueprint architecture is a constraint-driven,
self-stabilizing, and prevention-coupled process that reorganizes the system
to preserve coherence while expanding invariant structure.